Phillips and Mr Privet on equipment maintenance;
illustrated talks by Mrs Boydell on travel; by Miss B. Witts, Teddington Hospital, on electricity in physio-
therapy; by Mr Brodie entitled 'Building for the future';
and the annual luncheon when Mrs L. Speller spoke on
the experiences of her husband and herself as the first
Mayor and Mayoress of newly formed Elbridge.

Thanet had a talk on the Royal National Lifeboat
Institution; and a cookery demonstration by SEEB. Tunbridge Wells had illustrated talks entitled 'Reflec-
tions of Hastings Old Town; and 'The four seasons';
a breadmaking demonstration by Mrs Wells, SEEB;
and visited the Milne Museum of early electrical appli-
ances. Woking had talks by Mr R.

Luttman, SEB;
and a talk on the training and judging of dogs. Newbury had talks on the EEIBA by Mr Carver;
on the work of the British Red Cross Society;
demonstrations of cookery by SEB; of hairdressing
by Mr Kevin de Brett; and the films 'Helping hands'
and 'Frozen summer'. Oxford had demonstrations of microwave cookery;
floral art; and the film 'Alice in label-land'.

